\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Solar-derived kilonova composition ($X_{\rm  lan}=0.121$) at $t=1$~day: $\kappa _R^{\rm  exp}$ (left) and $\kappa _P^{\rm  tot}/\kappa _R^{\rm  exp}$ ratio (right). Density $10^{-16}$--$10^{-11}$~g/cm$^3$, the range spanned by the diffusion surface in the transport calculations of \secref  {SecRadiationSimulations}. The temperature range is cut at $2$~eV, above which the mean ionization saturates at the three-electron limit of our atomic data (see text). Both colorbars are clipped at both ends; within the plotted range $\kappa _R^{\rm  exp}$ spans $0.006$--$103$~cm$^2$/g and the ratio spans $1.6$--$132$.}}{7}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
